"yoy":1204.2}]},"year":{"label":"FY26","note":"EPS = exit-quarter annualised (not summed)","prior":"FY25","rows":[{"cur":182,"metric":"Revenue (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":146,"yoy":24.7},{"cur":11,"metric":"Operating Profit (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":20,"yoy":-45.0},{"cur":6.0,"metric":"OPM (%)","nd":1,"pct":true,"prior":13.7,"yoy":-7.7},{"cur":10,"metric":"PAT (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":12,"yoy":-16.7},{"cur":0.8,"metric":"EPS (Rs, annualised, exit qtr)","nd":2,"pct":false,"prior":-0.54,"yoy":-248.1}]}},"profile":{"entities":"Mold-Tek Technologies Ltd (Parent); Beryl Project Engineering (Subsidiary)","mgmt":"","subseg":"Structural Steel Detailing; Structural Design; Mechanical Engineering (Poles/Towers); Residential Inspection & Permitting","themes":"Turnaround via BIW auto downsizing; US Grid/Tower ramp-up; Inorganic growth via Beryl acquisition"},"qtr":"Q4FY26","ratios":[{"label":"ROE %","value":"8.2%"},{"label":"ROCE %","value":"10.3%"},{"label":"D/E","value":"0.0x"},{"label":"Int cover","value":"21.7x"},{"label":"Receivable d","value":"83.9"},{"label":"OPM %","value":"6.3%"}],"s":"MOLDTECH","sec":"Engineering Design Services & Energy Transition Infrastructure","sec2":"Construction","sections":{"bull_bear":[{"body":"Zero debt; INR 25-30 Cr cash/deposits on books. Strategy: Inorganic growth via acquisitions (Beryl completed; high-rise design target in talks). Preferential issue of INR 164/share cancelled due to market price disconnect.","src":"concall","title":"Capital allocation"},{"body":"FX Volatility: INR 4 Cr MTM loss highlights hedging risks; US Recession/Rate impact on residential construction (Beryl); AI disruption perceived as low risk by mgmt but could reduce headcount needs; Client concentration in US utilities.","src":"concall","title":"Risks & watch-items"},{"body":"Candid on past failures (auto segment bleed); Confident on turnaround mechanics; Defensive on acquisition strategy (strategic vs desperate); Transparent on accounting distortions (MTM, acquisition costs).","src":"concall","title":"Management quality / tone"},{"body":"The 'loss' in Q4 was largely accounting noise (MTM hedging loss + prior quarter acquisition costs); Operational EBITDA is recovering. The BIW auto segment alone caused a INR 7-8 Cr annual drag which is now fully eliminated from FY27 onwards.","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"}],"business":[{"body":"Civil Services: 90% detailing, 10% design (targeting 30-40% design mix in 3-4 years). Mechanical Services: Exited bleeding BIW auto (Tesla/BMW suppliers); pivoting to US utility poles/towers/substations (80-90% US exposure). Beryl (US Subs): 5-month contribution; INR 23 Cr annualized revenue; 80% permitting/inspection, 20% design.","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| US Grid modernization and pole replacement cycle accelerating demand for engineering design | Mold-Tek Technologies Ltd | beneficiary | High | Direct ramp in poles/towers segment ($1M to $2M projected) offsets auto decline; zero debt allows aggressive hiring. |\n| Slowdown in EV new model launches reducing BIW engineering needs | Pure-play Auto Engineering Firms | loser | Med | Mold-Tek exited this space; competitors still exposed to the INR 7-8 Cr industry-wide drag. |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"Beryl margins: 8-10% (limited by inspection-heavy mix). Core India Engineering margins: Expected to rebound to 15-16% EBITDA after removing INR 7 Cr auto loss. Cost base: Wage-heavy; hedging policy revised to cover only 25-50% of exposure to avoid MTM volatility.","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"Revenue: FY27 target INR 250 Cr (implied by Q4 annualized run-rate). Margins: EBITDA margin guidance 15% (up from ~11% FY26), driven by mix shift to design and removal of auto losses. Order Inflow: Civil Structural work on hand up 70% to $5 Mn; Poles/Towers revenue expected to double to $1.5-2 Mn.","src":"concall","title":"Guidance"},{"body":"Civil Structural (CES): $5 Mn (up from $2.84 Mn); Mechanical (MES): $0.25 Mn (down from $0.5 Mn, post-auto exit).","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"Cross-selling Beryl's US sales team to sell Mold-Tek's core steel detailing/design; Outsourcing 50% of Beryl's non-inspection work to India to expand margins; Potential high-rise design acquisition in Atlanta; New MSA with Danieli Corus ($0.5 Mn potential).","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["Q4FY26 concall summary","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"Mold-Tek executed a strategic pivot in Q4FY26 by slashing loss-making BIW auto headcount (160 to 60) while ramping US pole/tower work, driving a Q4 profit turnaround to INR 2.28 Cr despite INR 4 Cr FX MTM losses. The acquisition of Beryl adds a new residential design/inspection vertical, positioning the company for a FY27 revenue target of INR 250 Cr with expanded margin potential from higher-value design services.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":0.0,"fy":"FY22","mcap":228,"opm":23.2,"pe":17.1,"roe":19.9},{"de":0.0,"fy":"FY23","mcap":689,"opm":30.2,"pe":23.5,"roe":33.2},{"de":0.0,"fy":"FY24","mcap":516,"opm":27.7,"pe":18.6,"roe":24.8},{"de":0.0,"fy":"FY25","mcap":425,"opm":16.2,"pe":34.8,"roe":10.2},{"de":0.04,"fy":"FY26","mcap":346,"opm":6.3,"pe":34.3,"roe":8.2}],"wtt":null},"drhp":{"rpt":{"financials":{"_source":"ledger","balance_sheet_key":[{"basis":"Consolidated","cwip_amount_rs":0,"equity_share_capital_amount_rs":55700000,"fy":"FY2019","inventory_amount_rs":0,"net_fixed_assets_amount_rs":183600000,"networth_amount_rs":506900000,"other_equity_amount_rs":451200000,"total_assets_amount_rs":615800000,"trade_payables_amount_rs":14200000,"trade_receivables_amou